Time Complexity:

Let n = length of string

    Single traversal → O(n)
    Building result → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity:

    Stack stores characters → O(n)
    StringBuilder → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Approach:

1. Create a stack to store characters

2. Push first character into stack

3. Traverse the string:
   - If current character is different from top of stack:
     → push it into stack
   - Else:
     → skip (ignore consecutive duplicate)

4. After traversal:
   - Pop all elements from stack and add to StringBuilder

5. Reverse the result (since stack is LIFO)

6. Return final string





class Solution {
    public String removeConsecutiveCharacter(String s) {
        Stack<Character> st = new Stack<>();
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        st.push(s.charAt(0));
        for(int i=0; i<s.length(); i++){
            if(st.peek()!=s.charAt(i)) st.push(s.charAt(i));
        }
        while(st.size()!=0){
            sb.append(st.pop());
        }
        return sb.reverse().toString();
    }
}
